message:
Added additional positional graph sanity checking with error messages;
Lowered default throttling threshold
Removed realignment debugging message spam

make collection chain a string early

Numpy recently added a deprecation warning for "ragged" arrays;
in this case it was ragged because of a type mismatch;
CollectionSearch vs str. Making the CollectionSearch a string
in the list comprehension prevents us from encountering the
warning.

Remove old instructions about registry/datastore changes.

The changes directory no longer divides change reports by component;
they all go in the same directory.

Fix Query references to datasets (not types).

Some of the Query documentation conflated datasets with dataset types;
I've tried to correct the references.

Switch SQLAlchemy import style.

I think I swung too far in the direction of 'from X import Y' before;
a lot of these very short symbols really need namespace context.

Make DataCoordinate has* flags into properties.

This is a type of change I normally would resist making, but...

 - I'd really like to start using properties for cases like this in
 future classes (in part to align myself better with what I see the
 rest of the dev team doing);

 - I'd really like to start using snake_case in new classes;

 - I'd like to start doing both in classes that will have their own
 versions of these exact state flags, so the inconsistency would be
 more jarring than usual if I left them as-is;

 - By adding snake_case properties, I can leave camelCase methods for
 for backwards compatibility.  I'm changing everything in daf_butler,
 but I don't want to go beyond that on this ticket if I can avoid it.

Use alternates in file template and merge some options

{exposure.obs_id}_{group} -> {exposure.obs_id|group}
{visit.day_obs}/{exposure.day_obs} -> {day_obs|visit.day_obs|exposure.day_obs}
